  "source_and_cpu_notes": [
    "The original R18 ALP+ZSTD3 versus ZSTD1 changed two variables at once, not a pure test of ALP's CPU or compression benefit. This 2x2 controls level when removing ALP and controls ALP when changing level.",
    "In entropy `pod_namespace`, remove ALP holding ZSTD3: QueryFinish CPU111.914->102.548ms (-8.4%) with A/A CPU drift0.74%; SAMPLES compressed bytes19,686,139->20,216,284 (+2.69%). Entropy burst15 CPU74.499->66.506ms (-10.7%) with 4.90% A/A CPU drift.",
    "On original repeating gauges at ZSTD3, removing ALP changes CPU in `pod_namespace` by just+0.09% with 7.08% control drift even though storage shrinks36.7%; a previous unreplicated +10% namespace CPU penalty from simultaneously changing ALP+level cannot be called a stable per-ALP effect.",
    "Representative high-entropy `pod_namespace` ALP+ZSTD3 query trace CPU folded stacks include 18 of110 samples with `CompressionCodecALP` in stack; matched raw ZSTD3 has zero of102. For burst15 ALP10/84 vs raw0/66. These sampled stacks are per one query, not numerical attribution of the full median CPU difference.",
    "Compression level3->1 changes storage by+4.66% with ALP and+1.75% without ALP for patterned values, but on high-entropy values all level1 and level3 SAMPLES bytes are identical within ALP/no-ALP group. CPU/latency level effects are usually small relative to control drift.",
    "Even a statistically notable local CPU improvement from removing ALP does not establish global performance gain on a mixed production metric corpus. Workloads with different entropy, timestamp layout, high-cardinality queries, late points and merging vary."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "All values synthetic; original 400-node starts aligned to 3h boundaries. High-entropy deterministic SplitMix64 finite Float64 in[0,1), no NaN/Inf/counter reset or staleness.",
    "Source binary LLVM22 -O1 glibc; no equal optimized jemalloc O2/O3 ClickHouse versus VM parity. Previously running jemalloc build must not be cancelled.",
    "One unpaired bulk insert and one OPTIMIZE per codec. Physical disk byte measurements valid, but writer CPU/merge effects are not steady-state paired proofs.",
    "Only one native client under factorial; 1/4/8-client read test exists separately for ALPZSTD3 versus raw ZSTD1 and does not isolate ALP alone. Do not combine CPU from different CI runners.",
    "CPU trace samples are representative statistical samples and cannot be treated as a mutex/critical path proof."
  ]
